exit: Some(0)
--- stdout ---
Extend the chain: hash the program, chain onto the current tip, append, and print the new `entry_hash`. Refuses (exit 15) if the existing chain at `--store` fails verification against the genesis before appending

Usage: axon-vm chain stamp [OPTIONS] --prog <PROG> --store <STORE>

Options:
      --prog <PROG>      Path to the .ax program being run (its SHA-256 is chained in)
      --run-id <RUN_ID>  Run-id for this stamp. If omitted, a process-id + monotonic-clock id is generated (same scheme `axon-vm run` uses for its own run_id)
      --store <STORE>    Path to the chain JSONL file (created if absent)
      --kernel <KERNEL>  Guest kernel image used to derive the R31 genesis root (default: dist/guest/vmlinuz). Only consulted when the chain is empty
  -h, --help             Print help

